# Declared RLS test files, one per line. '#' starts a comment.
#
# The runner reconciles this list against supabase/tests/rls/*.sql before it
# runs anything, and fails in both directions:
#
#   - a file listed here but missing from the directory  -> FAIL
#   - a .sql file in the directory but not listed here   -> FAIL
#
# The first catches a test that was deleted or never delivered. Without it a
# suite that shrank to nothing still reports "passed" and exit 0, which is
# indistinguishable from a full pass -- the gate could not tell "everything
# passed" from "almost nothing ran".
#
# The second catches a file arriving undeclared, which is how a stray probe or
# a half-finished test slips into a green run.
#
# Declaring a test is therefore a deliberate act. Adding a test file means
# adding a line here.

